BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Asian Heritage Month Clay Animals!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T150000
UID:69dffd3a4dacf581ff8904ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pandas!  Snakes! Tigers!  What are the animals of Asia? Learn 
 how to make cute clay animals and all about Asian countries and culture.\n
 For children ages 5-12 with parents or caregivers.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dffd3a4dacf581ff8904ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
