BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Public Health: Managing Stress-Children
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T120000
UID:69ea4e4f2866a5b4884a6537@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will help participants understand the different 
 kinds of stress\, explain what happens to children's bodies and minds duri
 ng stress and how to identify signs and symptoms of stress in young childr
 en. It will also provide strategies to help children cope with and manage 
 stress.\nThis workshop is intended for parents and/or caregivers. Children
  under the age of 6 are welcome.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ea4e4f2866a5b4884a6537
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
