BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rabbit and Bear Paws Puppet Show: The Way
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T150000
UID:69ef93e81e64afd01e6bf96b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This interactive puppet show from Chad Solomon features chara
 cters from the\nRabbit and Bear Paws\nchildren's graphic novel series. In 
 this performance\, audiences will experience the story of how the turtle
  carried our world on her back\, and how the tiny muskrat succeeded in giv
 ing us the greatest gift of all - a place to call home\, Turtle Island.\nC
 had Solomon\nis a member of the Henvey Inlet\, First Nation. As a child\, 
 he would visit with his late grandparents. Chad's grandfather\, a tradit
 ional healer and justice activist\, taught him that no matter how old you 
 become\, you should always be young-at-heart and that laughter is the grea
 test medicine. This is the spirit behind the comical Adventures of Rabbit 
 and Bear Paws series.\nThis event is apart of the "Riverside Eats & Beats 
 Street fest" on Queen from the Riverside Bridge to just past Degrassi St.
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ef93e81e64afd01e6bf96b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
